                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a 4/10 game. Or, calling it a game is a bit generous. it's more of a \"Run Back and Forth\"-simulator and a more proper title than Greedfall would be Fetch Quest Simulator. This game has zero value, so even buying it at 90% off on sale is a waste of your money, but first hand a waste of your finite time here on earth. It's shallow, underdeveloped, insanely repetitive, and the world is more or less dead, with NPC's just standing around waiting for you. There's in total three different environments that are reused from star to finish. The combat is simplistic and boring. The RPG systems are mostly there for show and has no real consequences. Your build has no narrative impact. The script is tedious and infantile, the dialogues are boring and written by a midwit. Unmemorable characters and two-dimensional characterization. Awful party banter. The music is lifeless. \n\nEverything, and I mean everything, is generic and predictable. About halfway through you'll notice there's no reason to pick up loot from one of the 5 different monsters there are in total. \n\nThis game is lifeless, static and dead, and I just can't take it anymore. I'm closing in on the end, but I just can't see this through.",
